<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Intentionally EMPTY of definitions.

  This file was created while fixing the app's missing styles, on the assumption
  that the API-31-plus folder was the right home for the `AppTheme` alias the
  manifest points at. It is not: `AppTheme` is the theme of the whole app and
  lives in the default values/themes.xml, so that API 24 (the app's minSdk) is
  themed as well. Defining it only here would have left every device below API 31
  with no theme at all.

  It is kept rather than deleted, because removing a tracked file is a change
  someone else should agree to, and it documents why nothing belongs here. The
  genuinely API-31-specific theme work already has its own file:
  values-v31/themes.xml, which overrides `Theme.MindsetFrames` to add the Android
  12 splash-screen items. `AppTheme` inherits from that one, so it picks those up
  automatically on API 31+ without a copy being kept here.
-->
<resources />
